{"seq": 19, "tool": "submit", "kind": "terminal", "args": {"decision": "fix_config", "root_cause": "monitor:freshness_raw_payments", "evidence": ["ALR-58947E", "ALR-786411", "get_calendar: 2026-11-11 is Veterans Day, not a business day", "payments contract: no file is delivered for bank holidays; holiday payments roll into the next business day's file", "landing/payments has no files for earlier holidays either (20260907, 20261012), and the 2026-11-10 file arrived on time and loaded (280 rows)", "harbor_daily runs for ds 2026-11-10 succeeded (tr-000269..tr-000272); no run for the holiday", "monitors.yml: both freshness monitors used calendar=weekdays (only knows weekends), so they expected a 2026-11-11 partition", "config commits eb3aa1c5, 2a785c0e set calendar=business_calendar"], "summary": "Both freshness alerts were false positives. The monitors expected a 2026-11-11 partition, but that day was Veterans Day. Under its contract, Keel does not send a payments file on bank holidays, so there was no 2026-11-11 partition for raw.payments or mart_delinquency. All data up to 2026-11-10 loaded and published normally, and nothing is missing. The two monitors used the 'weekdays' calendar, which only knows weekends. I switched both to 'business_calendar', which also knows bank holidays, and that cleared both alerts. No backfill or escalation is needed."}, "ok": true, "error": null, "result_chars": 47, "duration_ms": 0.2, "sim_now": "2026-11-12 08:30:20"}
